INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,url_slug,status,updated_at,created_at) VALUES
('wholesale','Wholesale','outsider','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"wholesale","name":"Wholesale","team":"outsider","ability":"The 1st (& only) time an evil player chooses to discard their vote token (secretly), they can make a wish, even if you''re dead.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Wholesale (SCP-2855 - a.k.a Mr. Money) can be whatever the buyer wants it to be.","summaryBullets":["The Wholesale allows for an impure dead to purchase them with their Obol.","If on the script, evil players are allowed to make a wish at the cost of discarding their vote token entirely, removing their last chance to vote while dead.","Vote tokens attained or used by other sources {{i|(like the Beggar)}} are applicable here.","If an evil player does discard their vote token, no one immediately learns this. They may still pretend to use a vote token despite having used it.","Like the Legion, if an evil player''s use of their imaginary vote token causes a change in execution status, the false result is publicly declared, whilst the real result is secretly kept.","And like the Wizard or Puzzlemaster, an evil player''s ability to disregard their vote token and make their wish has no limitations on when this occur - they can do this publicly, private, during the day, or during the night.","If an evil player does discard their vote token but the Wholesale ability isn''t in-play, they learn nothing.","If an evil player would discard their vote token but another evil player had already done so, the vote token is not discard.","Otherwise, if the evil player successfully makes the wish using the vote token they discard, they learn they gained a wish.","The Storyteller may alert the player that they gained a wish, but that it is not granted for whatever reason, and that they should try again with another.","When an evil player makes their wish, the Storyteller may choose to interpret the wish differently in order to make it balanced for both teams.","However, these wishes will typically not come with any price or clue to it''s nature."],"howToRun":["At any time during the game, either verbally or via text, a dead evil player may choose to secretly discard their vote token and make a wish if no evil player has the **BROKE** reminder token present on them, even if the Wholesale is not in-play. If so, they secretly lose a vote token - mark them with the **BROKE** reminder token. When running the vote tally, if the evil player pretends to use their vote token despite not having it, publicly announce the vote result as normal, but secretly keep of a record of which player is really about to die by marking them with the **ABOUT TO DIE** reminder, then execute them when nominations are over.","If the Wholesale is in-play, decide whether to accept or decline the wish. If the wish is declined, prompt the evil player to wish again when they can.","Once granted, say “**Your wish is granted.**” or “**Your wish is my command**”, or nod, or otherwise signal that their wish is accepted. Use the Wholesale’s **?** reminders if needed, to substitute for the wish’s own reminders."],"tips":["Be cautious about what power, boon, or benefit you give to the wisher of the Wholesale. There is no guarantee for any modicum of a clue or drawback to arrive - albeit no restriction saying that there can''t be. So be very cautious about using this Outsider in comparison to the roster of other character types, and what you do grant in the end."],"quote":"I looked up in the sky last night and all the stars were shining bright, I wished I may and I wished I might just have the wish I wished last night.","iconBy":"le_nuberto","customBoxes":[{"title":"Alternative JSON & How to Run (Older)","content":"If you want to use the older version of the Wholesale, where a player purchased for their allegiance with their ability, use this JSON.\n\nWhile preparing the first night, put the Wholesale''s **ODD** reminder token by the Wholesale''s character token, and you may choose to rotate the Wholesale''s character token. Do not wake the Wholesale to let them know their current alignment.\n\nEach dusk, replace the Wholesale''s **ODD** reminder token with the **EVEN** reminder token, and vice-versa.\n\nThe first time you hear the Wholesale agree a request to join an asking player''s alignment, rotate the Wholesale’s character token - right side up for good, upside-down for evil - to match this asking player''s alignment. Mark the Wholesale with the **SOLD** reminder, and mark the asking player with the **BUYER** reminder.\n\nThe player marked with the **BUYER** reminder is drunk every night if they''re a Townsfolk, or they''re drunk every odd-numbered night if they''re a Minion.\n\nRemember to keep the Wholesale''s ability when they die and to have their reminder tokens persist.\n\n**Wholesale █~** (Outsider)\nYou join 1st player you agree to''s team, who is drunk each night (if Townsfolk), or even night (if Minion), even if dead. [You might secretly start evil.]\n\n**Reminders:** Even, Odd, Sold, Buyer\n**Setup:** yes\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch. Image: @le_nuberto\n\n**Jinxes:**\nBoffin: If the Demon has the Wholesale ability, they can’t turn good due to this ability.\nPit-Hag: If the Pit-Hag turns an evil player into the Wholesale, they can''t turn good due to their own ability.\nHuli Jing: If the Huli Jing gains the Wholesale ability, they can not turn Good.\nDon Juan: An evil Wholesale doesn''t register as an Outsider for the Don Juan''s ability.\nModiste: If the Modiste gains the Wholesale ability, they can not turn Good."}],"firstNight":0,"otherNight":16.2855,"reminders":["?","?","?"],"remindersGlobal":["Broke","About to die"],"setup":false,"otherNightReminder":"If the evil player''s wish requires action at night, run these.","art":"art/wholesale.png","jsonId":"wholesale_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/wholesale','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('c-insurgency','C-Insurgency','outsider','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"c-insurgency","name":"C-Insurgency","team":"outsider","ability":"If a player causes or attempts something bad to happen to you, your alignment becomes that opposing them (unless killed).","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The C-Insurgency constantly defects to different sides.","summaryBullets":["At any time, if a player does something bad to the C-Insurgency, whether it was through their ability, someone else''s ability, or by nominating them, the C-Insurgency immediately defects against their side.","At night, just before dawn, the C-Insurgency wakes to know what their resulting alignment is, even if they died in between the alignment change and them learning it.","The C-Insurgency does not change their alignment when dead.","The C-Insurgency will change their alignment when made drunk or poisoned, and then will remain drunk or poisoned for the specified duration.","The C-Insurgency will defect against a player if the {{i|attempt}} to do something bad to them, but it fails, such as being drunk or poisoned, or if the effects of an ability fail due to the C-Insurgency not meeting a certain condition."],"howToRun":["When the C-Insurgency is nominated, drunken-ed, poisoned, inflicted with any other negative status effect {{i|(whether it occurs or is attempted)}}, or attempted to be killed by another player, if that player’s alignment is the same the C-Insurgency’s alignment, rotate the C-Insurgency’s character token—right side up for good, upside-down for evil—to oppose that player’s alignment. If made drunk or poisoned, you will still rotate the C-Insurgency character token to oppose that player, but any further rotations won''t occur until the C-Insurgency is sober and healthy. Lastly, \"attempts to be killed by another player\" include kills that were prevented by being unable to die, or abilities with kills targeting the C-Insurgency that either failed due to drunk or poisoning, or by a certain condition not being met {{i|(ex. Slayer shot counts as an attempt to kill the C-Insurgency)}}, but the C-Insurgency does not change their alignment if they are successfully killed however.","Each night except the first, wake the C-Insurgency, even if they just died. Give them a thumbs-up or a thumbs-down {{i|(indicating their current alignment)}}. Put the C-Insurgency to sleep."],"tips":["Before running a game with the C-Insurgency, clarify what notable interactions are possible with them as to avoid confusion and bring players up to speed with how the game theory changes with this new information, alongside the basic always active activates-on-nomination event."],"quote":"Wow, thank you for attempting to discharge your weapon in front of your superior and commanding officer. I''ll be sure to amend this piece of fine history on my auto-biography and on your obituary, jackass.","iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Boffin","align":"evil","text":"If the Demon has the C-Insurgency ability, they can’t turn good due to this ability.","id":"boffin"},{"name":"Pit-Hag","align":"evil","text":"If the Pit-Hag turns an evil player into the C-Insurgency, they can''t turn good due to their own ability.","id":"pithag"},{"name":"Huli Jing","align":"evil","text":"If the Huli-Jing has the C-Insurgency ability, they can not turn Good.","id":"hulijing_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Don Juan","align":"evil","text":"An evil C-Insurgency doesn''t register as an Outsider for the Don Juan''s ability.","id":"donjuan_darkartists_stuff"},{"name":"Modiste","align":"evil","text":"If the Modiste gains the C-Insurgency ability, they can not turn Good.","id":"modiste_darkartists_stuff"}],"firstNight":0,"otherNight":89.1593,"setup":false,"otherNightReminder":"Show them the thumbs up good signal or the thumbs down evil signal accordingly, even if they''re dead.","art":"art/c-insurgency.png","jsonId":"cinsurgency_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/c-insurgency','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('duende','Duende','outsider','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"duende","name":"Duende","team":"outsider","ability":"You start knowing a question. Each day or night*, privately answer it: if correct, you see the Grimoire & turn evil.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Duende scavenges for things to steal, and - if crafty - uncovers the booty of the Grimoire.","summaryBullets":["The Duende starts knowing a question, and nothing else. Should they correctly answer it, they gain the benefit of seeing into the Grimoire, and becoming evil.","Nothing bad happens to the good team should the Duende fail to answer their question at all whilst they live.","It is Duende''s choice to answer their question, should they decide they want to remain good and not risk being evil.","The Duende can answer once per day, or night. They only wake at night to answer if they didn''t do so during the day, and the type of question they have can permit a silent answer during the night.","The Duende effectively knows if they are incorrect in their answer, since they won''t plunder any rewards on failure {{i|(unless drunk or poisoned)}}.","Jinxes involving the Duende seeing into the Grimoire should be less severe against them."],"howToRun":["During setup, write a question on a piece of paper, or on a phone.","During the first night, wake the Duende. Show this question, then put them to sleep.","Once per day, if the Duende requests a private chat with you, take them away from the circle so you cannot be overheard. They give their answer. If incorrect, mark them with the **INCORRECT** reminder token.","Each night except the first, if the Duende''s question or the game''s medium permits them to answer silently during the night and they are not marked with the **INCORRECT** reminder token, wake them. Show them the question again, then they give the signals necessary to answer it. Afterwards, put them to sleep.","Each dawn, remove the **INCORRECT** reminder token if its present.","If the Duende answers correctly, jackpot! Show them the “You Are” info token, and a thumbs down. Show them the Grimoire for as long as they need."],"tips":["The Duende should generally be given a question that can only leave them with a 5% to 10% or less chance of guessing successfully if going by random chance alone and nothing else."],"quote":"> wife pregnant for 8 months\n> her water breaks, rush her to hospital\n> she goes into intensive labour & passes away due to complications\n> doctor hands me what came out of womb\n> 2 gold Örtugs, a dead chicken, and 1 I.O.U\n> fucking duendes","iconBy":"Game-icons.net","jinxes":[{"name":"Damsel","align":"good","text":"When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Damsel is poisoned.","id":"damsel"},{"name":"Heretic","align":"good","text":"When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Heretic is poisoned.","id":"heretic"},{"name":"Abdominal","align":"good","text":"Only 1 jinxed character can be in play.","slug":"abdominal"},{"name":"xX_2662_Xx","align":"evil","text":"Instead of adding 1 Outsider, 1 Townsfolk is secretly drunk. When the Duende views the Grimoire, they see xX_2662_Xx as the Demon whose ability they have and doesn''t know who is secretly drunk.","slug":"xx-2662-xx"},{"name":"Wig Snatcher","align":"good","text":"The Wig Snatcher cannot become the Duende.","id":"wigsnatcher_hblreleased"},{"name":"Au’Wre","align":"evil","text":"If Au’Wre is in play, the Duende only sees half of the Grimoire.","id":"auwre_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Ketos","align":"evil","text":"If Ketos is in play, the Duende learns all in-play characters & evil players instead of seeing the Grimoire.","id":"ketos_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Visionary","align":"evil","text":"When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Visionary is poisoned.","id":"visionary_the_bootleggers_anthology"}],"customBoxes":[{"title":"Credit","content":"Ability: @legitch. Image: Game-icons.net"},{"title":"Alternative JSON & How to Run (Older)","content":"If you want to use the older version of the Duende, where it also transformed into a Minion upon a correct answer of their question, use this JSON. Arguably much stronger and detrimental the good team upon their transformation, use at your own risk.\n\nDuring setup, write a question on a piece of paper, or on a phone.\n\nDuring the first night, wake the Duende. Show this question, then put them to sleep.\n\nOnce per day, if the Duende requests a private chat with you, take them away from the circle so you cannot be overheard. They give their answer. If incorrect, mark them with the **INCORRECT** reminder token.\n\nEach night except the first, if the Duende''s question or the game''s medium permits them to answer silently during the night and they are not marked with the **INCORRECT** reminder token, wake them. Show them the question again, then they give the signals necessary to answer it. Afterwards, put them to sleep.\n\nEach dawn, remove the **INCORRECT** reminder token if its present.\n\nIf the Duende answers correctly, jackpot! Replace their old character token with a Minion token, show them the “You Are” info token then the Minion character token, and give a thumbs down. Show them the Grimoire for as long as they need.\n\nIf the Duende transforms into an evil Minion already in-play and you don''t have duplicate character tokens for this Minion, you may instead flip the Duende''s character token upside-down {{i|(to indicate to yourself that they are evil)}} and mark the current Minion with the **USES MINION OF** reminder, to indicate that they are effectively this Minion. Use the Duende''s **?** reminders if needed, to substitute for the Minion''s own reminders.\n\n**Duende █+** (Outsider)\nYou start knowing a question. Each day or night*, privately answer it: if correct, you see the Grimoire & become an evil Minion.\n\n**First night:** Show the Duende their question.\n**Other nights:** You may show the Duende their question if it can be answered tonight. The Duende shows the signals needed to answer it. If correct, change their token to a Minion token. Show them the ''You Are'' card, the Minions they have become, a thumbs down, and then the Grimoire for as long as they need.\n**Reminders:** Incorrect, Uses Minion of, ?, ?, ?\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch. Image: Game-icons.net\n\n**Jinxes:**\nDamsel: When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Damsel is poisoned.\nHeretic: When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Heretic is poisoned.\nAbdominal: Only 1 jinxed character can be in play.\nxX_2662_Xx: Instead of adding 1 Outsider, 1 Townsfolk is secretly drunk. When the Duende views the Grimoire, they see xX_2662_Xx as the Demon whose ability they have and doesn''t know who is secretly drunk.\nWig Snatcher: The Wig Snatcher cannot become the Duende.\nAu’Wre: If Au’Wre is in play, the Duende only sees half of the Grimoire.\nKetos: If Ketos is in play, the Duende learns all in-play characters & evil players instead of seeing the Grimoire.\nVisionary: When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Visionary is poisoned."}],"firstNight":12.33,"otherNight":25.33,"reminders":["Incorrect"],"setup":false,"firstNightReminder":"Show the Duende their question.","otherNightReminder":"You may show the Duende their question if it can be answered tonight. The Duende shows the signals needed to answer it. If correct, show them the ''You Are'' card, a thumbs down, and then the Grimoire for as long as they need.","art":"art/duende.png","jsonId":"duende_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/duende','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));
